        HelpEntry(
            id = "shut-down",
            title = "Shut down the day",
            keywords = listOf("shut down the day", "shut down", "shutdown", "done for the day", "end of day", "wake alarm", "how are you feeling", "tired", "stretched", "lighten tomorrow", "shattered", "hold alerts", "see tomorrow", "tomorrow's tasks", "tomorrow peek", "swipe to tomorrow", "edit tomorrow's task"),
            what = "an evening moment: what got done, what carries over to tomorrow, tomorrow's first thing and the wake alarm.",
            how = "It comes as a card at work's end (20:00 on other days); open it and tap Shut down.",
            tips = listOf("The wake alarm it suggests counts the commute and your time to get ready.", "On the Fold it can end with a photo from this date in past years (On this day): Turn on at the bottom of the pane. The photo stays on the phone.", "Before an office day, Tomorrow names your first train and when to leave for it (\"First train · the 07:42 · leave by 07:32\"), from the train you caught on recent mornings, with how it has run. It needs Home station and Time to the train in About you.", "Not ready yet? Later on the card (or its heads-up) puts it off an hour, never past 23:00. Turn off at the foot of the pane stops the evening card and its heads-up for good (the pane still opens from Ask → Daily); on annual leave days it doesn't come unless you open it.", "Say \"shut down the day\" to Talk to open it. On the Galaxy Watch the evening shows \"6 done · 2 left for tomorrow\" with Shut down and Later.", "How are you feeling? Pick Good, Tired or Stretched. Tired offers to lighten tomorrow, moving up to two of its tasks (evening ones first) to lighter days; Stretched also names one that could wait on Someday. Nothing moves until you tap, with Undo, and how you felt stays on that device only, for a week.", "Or just tell Obi: \"I'm shattered\", \"I'm knackered\" or \"I've got too much on\" keeps how you feel and he says what he'd move; the taps wait in Shut down the day. Stretched can also hold mail and call alerts that can wait (the ten-minute inbox, parcels, notes about strangers' calls) for a day; urgent calls and Always notify still come through, and Resume ends it.", "To see tomorrow, swipe left across Today on the Fold or tap the date under the greeting (any time), or from 5pm tap the Tomorrow card on Today (\"Tomorrow · Thu 22 Oct · 2 tasks · first 07:40 Gym\"); swipe right to come back. Tick a task there, or move it to Today or the Day after; its time comes with it.", "In Tomorrow, tap a task (or Edit) to change its title, time, reminder, repeat, notes or checklist, as on Today. A task you ask Obi to add for tomorrow is there, and Shut down counts it (\"1 planned for tomorrow\").", "Bills and renewals due tomorrow from Lists → Renewals show in Tomorrow (\"Due tomorrow · Water bill £32.50\"), and a last day to cancel shows in gold; the Tomorrow card counts them (\"1 bill due\").", "Lessons you planned for tomorrow (press and hold a lesson in a course under Goals) show in Tomorrow (\"Study · 2 lessons · about 1 h\"), and the Tomorrow card counts them (\"2 lessons to study\")."),
            fold = HelpPlace.SHUTDOWN,
            foldWhere = "Ask → Daily → Shut down the day",
            mac = HelpPlace.SHUTDOWN,
            macWhere = "Ask → Daily → Shut down the day",
            macHow = null,
        ),
        HelpEntry(
            id = "spam-calls",
            title = "Spam protection",
            keywords = listOf("spam calls", "spam call", "reported number", "scam number", "spam protection", "block a number", "block number", "blocked calls", "blocked numbers", "unblock", "caller id"),
            what = "numbers people online report as a scam, numbers your network couldn't verify, strangers who call twice in a week without a message and strangers who hang up on the call assistant are blocked, so they don't ring.",
            how = "It's always on while Navilife is the phone's Caller ID & spam app. Each block comes with Undo, and Activity → Blocked calls lists them with Unblock.",
            tips = listOf("Contacts, anyone you called in 90 days and emergency numbers are never blocked.", "Allow Navilife to read contacts and the call log, or repeat callers and hang-ups can't be caught.", "Android's own Blocked numbers list isn't used: Navilife's screening keeps the call from ringing instead.", "An unknown caller's number is looked up on the web: a reported scam is blocked, a sales caller goes to your call assistant, and the notification says what people reported.", "Your call assistant first asks who's calling: someone who says they're from the police, a bank or HMRC and asks for money or your details is told you'll contact the organisation directly, the call ends, and the number goes on Suspected spam for you to Block.", "When a caller who said who they are tells the assistant it's urgent, it rings your mobile from its own number: you hear who it is and what they said, and press 1 to take the call. Add Your mobile in About you to turn it on; nobody claiming to be the police, a bank or HMRC is ever put through.", "Turn on Screen unknown callers all the time (Work mode → Call assistant) and numbers you don't know go to the call assistant in the evening and at weekends too; family, contacts and anyone calling twice within 3 minutes still ring.", "When a number you don't know rings through, a warning shows over the call screen and on the lock screen: never give card details or PINs, or move money; hang up and call 101 or the number on your card from another phone. With earbuds in, Obi says it too.", "After a call from a number you don't know, Navilife asks \"Was that a scam?\": Scam blocks it and offers Report to Action Fraud or a text to 7726, Block just blocks it, and Fine means it won't ask about that number again. Activity → Calls asks the same.", "A number that looks like a police, bank or HMRC switchboard (the same exchange as the real one) gets \"Could be spoofed\" on the call warning, even if it is saved in your contacts: scammers fake those numbers. Add your own police force's and bank's switchboards in About you → Official numbers (\"police 01632 960000, bank 0306 999 0000\")."),
            fold = HelpPlace.WORK,
            foldWhere = "Ask → Settings → Work mode → Spam protection",
            mac = HelpPlace.ACTIVITY,
            macWhere = "Ask → Settings → Activity → Blocked calls",
            macHow = "The Mac lists the blocked numbers with Unblock; the blocking happens on the Fold.",
        ),
        HelpEntry(
            id = "speak-up",
            title = "Speaking up",
            keywords = listOf("speaking up", "obi in the car", "music turns down", "speak up", "speaks up", "says it out loud", "out loud", "obi talks", "obi speaks", "spoken alerts", "jarvis", "read alerts aloud", "mute obi", "shh", "urgent from family", "tomorrow stacking up", "busy tomorrow", "reply arrived", "they replied", "waiting for a reply", "focus", "do not disturb", "deep work", "breaks through", "liquidation said aloud", "approval running out"),
            what = "for a few moments that really matter, Obi says it out loud in a sentence or two, starting with your name: an urgent message from family or Always notify, money that can't wait, your train cancelled or 10 minutes or more late, time to leave for an event or booked session, once in the evening, that tomorrow is stacking up, and, if you turn it on, a reply you were waiting for.",
            how = "Each moment has its own switch there, all on to start except A reply you were waiting for. Obi only speaks through headphones, earbuds or the car (Bluetooth or Android Auto), on the bedside clock in the evening, or on the Mac while you're using it.",
            tips = listOf("Never out of the phone's own speaker, in quiet hours, in a meeting (an event with other people or a video link), in focus, on a call, or while you're talking to Obi; and never more than 6 a day (choose Up to 3 a day under How often).", "Focus is the Fold's Do Not Disturb, or a block on your calendar called Focus, Focus time, Deep work or Heads down.", "Money that can't wait (a payment or trade approval in its last 15 minutes, or a position near liquidation; never an amount) and Urgent from family break through focus, quiet hours and meetings, and don't count towards the day's limit; a call, a conversation with Obi, the phone's speaker and Mute still keep him quiet.", "Everything else that works in the background posts a card rather than talking, marked with what it asks of you: To know, Asks you, or Needs your yes.", "Mute for 2 hours keeps him quiet on every device; the notifications still arrive as usual. Saying \"shh\" or \"not now\" to Obi in Talk does the same.", "Urgent from family is said only for someone on your family or Always notify list whose message says it's urgent (strangers never), with the start of their words; it's the same alert work mode lets through.", "He only tells you: anything to do is the usual notification or card. Everything he says on his own is in Activity, marked Said aloud.", "A tap on the docked orb while he speaks stops him and says hello as usual. On the bedside clock its orb lights up as he speaks, and a tap there just stops him.", "Tomorrow stacking up comes at 19:30 the evening before a day with three or more things on it (tasks due, bills, carried tasks, evening events): \"Meka, tomorrow is stacking up: Trip form, Council tax and Gym. Today has a way to lighten it.\" It is a notification too, and Today's stacking-up line has the one-tap fix.", "A reply you were waiting for is off to start. When someone answers an email of yours on Waiting for, a notification \"Sam Taylor replied\" comes either way; turned on, Obi also says \"Meka, Sam Taylor replied to your email about Quote for the kitchen.\" within the hour. Only their name and your subject are said, never their words. Got it in Time to chase settles it.", "In the car with Android Auto (wired or wireless) he speaks through the car's speakers, and whatever is playing (music, a podcast) turns down while he speaks and comes back up as he finishes. The same with earbuds."),
            fold = HelpPlace.SPEAK_UP,
            foldWhere = "Ask → Settings → Speaking up",
            mac = HelpPlace.SPEAK_UP,
            macWhere = "Ask → Settings → Speaking up",
            macHow = "On the Mac he speaks only while you're using it (a key or the mouse touched in the last 2 minutes); the switches are the same as the phone's and follow you. Urgent from family is said by the Fold, where work mode's alert arrives.",
        ),
        HelpEntry(
            id = "talk",
            title = "Talk",
            keywords = listOf("talk", "talk to navilife", "obi", "hey obi", "talk to obi", "ada", "hey ada", "voice", "speak", "side button", "headphones", "hey navilife", "hello navilife", "greeting", "orb", "wake word", "microphone"),
            what = "talk to Obi, Navilife's assistant, instead of typing: it answers aloud and anything it proposes still waits for your yes.",
            how = "Tap the mic in Ask's field. Under Settings → Talk you can make the side button or your headphones' button start it, and have it listen when Navilife opens.",
            tips = listOf("Tap the orb while it speaks to interrupt.", "After Obi answers, the mic opens again by itself for about eight seconds (\"Go on, I'm listening\" under the orb), so you can just carry on talking without a tap. Say \"thanks, Obi\" or \"that's all\", or say nothing, and the conversation ends; talk over him any time to interrupt.", "With signal, Google's online speech (Apple's on the Mac) writes down what you say, so it understands you better; with no signal the device's own recogniser listens. It stops listening about a second after you finish, and Activity's \"Speech to Added\" line shows how quickly what you asked to add went in.", "Hello, Navilife: with nothing typed, Ask shows a gold constellation orb (points on a slowly turning sphere); tap it (click on the Mac) and Navilife greets you by name and says the few things that matter now (what's urgent, your next event or train, what's due today), then listens. It glows warm while something needs you.", "The orb shows what Navilife is doing: it turns slowly at rest, its points shiver as you speak, it tightens and spins with gold rings while it thinks, and pushes out with a ring round its middle as it talks, in time with Navilife's own voice (it only reads how loud the voice is); two amber comets circle it while something needs you. With reduced motion it holds still.", "On the Fold, the small gold orb in the middle of the bar at the bottom (between Needs you and Calendar on the open Fold) is there on every screen: tap it and Ask comes forward and greets you, or takes you back to a conversation that's running. It glows amber while something needs you.", "Tap the small gold orb in the bar and Navilife makes an entrance: the orb flies to the middle, the screen goes dark, its points scatter and fly back in with a gold shockwave, and it starts saying hello as it flies up, with the words under it. Tap anywhere to skip the rest of the animation; swipe down (or say \"thanks\") and it shrinks back into the bar.", "As Navilife says hello, the things it mentions rise in as cards round the orb: what needs you, your train with its live status, your next event, what your partner asked for. Tap one to go straight there. When an answer offers something to do, its card rises there too with its button; nothing happens until you tap it. On the Mac the greeting's cards rise under the Ask orb.", "Every hello is different: one of over seventy greetings for the time of day, Monday mornings, Fridays and weekends, always with your name and a question, never the same twice within ten hellos.", "Obi also writes a few fresh hellos of his own about once a week, in the background, so they keep surprising you. Nothing about you is sent to write them, each is checked on your device first (your name, a question, nobody else named, nothing private), and they count in Navilife's AI as Chat.", "The first hello of the day Obi says who he is (\"Morning, Alex. It's Obi.\"); tap again within ten minutes and it's \"Back again?\". He mentions at most one thing from your day; ask \"what's going on?\" for the rest.", "Obi notices the moment, once: back from the office on an office-day evening (\"Home from work?\"), a match just finished (\"How did the football go?\") or rain outside. The Fold and the Mac share which hellos were said, so they never repeat each other.", "Answer Obi's \"how are you?\" and he answers back like a person: \"good thanks, you?\", \"not bad\" or \"shattered, long day\" gets his own reply at once, then \"What can I do for you?\". Saying more (\"good thanks, what's on tomorrow?\") is a question as usual.", "On the first open of the morning a short version plays once, without speaking. On the Mac the orb gathers itself the same way before it greets you. With reduced motion it simply fades in.", "Say hello from anywhere: on the Fold standing half folded (the bedside clock) tap the orb beside the alarm line; on the Mac click Say hello at the foot of the sidebar or in the menu bar, or press ⌥Space when you've been away a couple of hours (otherwise ⌥Space just listens). The greeting also says when your partner has asked you for something.", "On the stand, a tap on the bedside orb (or “Hey Obi”) makes the same entrance from that orb over the clock, a calm fade instead in quiet hours, and shrinks back into it when you're done; the clock returns.", "Obi is Navilife's assistant: the orb and the voice you talk to.", "Say “Hey Obi” (or “Hello Obi”; “Hello Navilife” still works) to start: turn it on in Ask → More → Talk. The Fold listens for it only on its stand (the bedside clock) while charging and outside quiet hours; the Mac only while Navilife is in front. Your words are recognised on the device and never sent, and a line beside the orb shows while it listens.", "Back at the Mac after two hours or more, Navilife welcomes you back with what matters now (never in quiet hours or protected time). Press Esc or ⌥Space to skip it, or turn Welcome back off in Ask → More → Talk.", "A longer spoken answer starts as soon as its first sentence is ready: Navilife says that while it writes the rest, then carries on; talk over it and it stops and listens. Only its own words are said early, and anything it offers to do still waits for your yes."),
            fold = HelpPlace.TALK,
            foldWhere = "Ask → the mic in the field, or Ask → Settings → Talk for the side button",
            mac = HelpPlace.TALK,
            macWhere = "Ask → the mic in the field, or ⌥Space anywhere",
            macHow = "Click the mic in Ask's field or press ⌥Space; macOS asks for the microphone and speech recognition the first time.",
        ),
        HelpEntry(
            id = "train-queue",
            title = "Train queue",
            keywords = listOf("train queue", "for the train", "read later", "save for the train"),
            what = "links and podcasts saved for the commute, kept to read offline.",
            how = "Share a link to Navilife and choose For the train, or paste one in the queue; Done moves it to Done lately.",
            tips = listOf("On office-day mornings Today's header says how many are waiting. Once you're on your train (with Home station and Time to the train in About you) it says how long until you change: \"On the 07:42 · 16 min to … · 2 articles · Dune at 37%\".", "On Wi-Fi the Fold keeps up to 30 waiting articles to read without a signal and lets each go once it's done. One it couldn't keep (a paywall, an app-only page) says \"Online only\" and opens in the browser; podcasts open in your podcast app.", "On the Mac, select a link in any app and choose Services → Save for the train with Navilife."),
            fold = HelpPlace.TRAIN_QUEUE,
            foldWhere = "Ask → Daily → Train queue",
            mac = HelpPlace.TRAIN_QUEUE,
            macWhere = "Ask → Daily → Train queue",
            macHow = null,
            data = true,
        ),
        HelpEntry(
            id = "trips",
            title = "Trips",
            keywords = listOf("trips", "trip timeline", "bookings", "add a trip", "travel mode", "packing list", "trip list", "to pack", "to buy", "before we leave", "start from last trip", "copy lists", "save as a template", "trip template", "who's going", "leave time", "leave home", "reminder", "remind me", "the night before", "add to my trip list", "what's left to pack", "obi's suggestions", "suggestions", "what have I forgotten", "add all", "not now", "move to another group", "rename a group", "new group", "drag to another group", "drag a group", "delete a group", "reorder groups", "change an item"),
            what = "trips and their bookings, day by day.",
            how = "Type a trip with its dates (\"Barcelona 14–18 Nov\"), then each booking with its day, time and reference.",
            tips = listOf("Share a booking confirmation to Navilife and Handle this offers to add it to the right trip.", "Open a trip: TRAVEL DOCUMENTS lists the passports, ID and health cards in your Vault (a driving licence when a car is booked, and travel insurance) and says whether each lasts the trip; a passport with under six months left when you're back is lit. Open copy shows a kept copy after your fingerprint (Touch ID on the Mac), offline too. Ask \"are our passports OK for Barcelona?\" for the same answer.", "A trip's days count as away: no commute, train alerts or leave-by those days (an evening flight on the first day still lets you work it), Work reads \"Work while away\", nobody is asked to cover the school days, and the brief and the week ahead say where you are. Book annual leave as well if you won't be working.", "Times are as on your tickets: the way there is UK time, everything after it is local. When the trip's name is a place Navilife knows (\"Barcelona\", \"Tenerife\"), its row says how far the clocks are apart (\"1 h ahead of UK time\") and each booking there shows UK time beside it (\"18:20 · Flight BA479 · 17:20 UK time\").", "While you're away on a trip named after a place Navilife knows, the morning brief gives that place's weather instead of home's (\"In Barcelona today, 18–24°, clear\", in local time), and the day before you go it adds tomorrow's there, so you know what to pack. Only the place's name goes to the weather service, as with home.", "Removed a booking or a trip by mistake? Tap Undo on the line that says what went (it stays a few seconds). A week after a trip ends it moves under PAST TRIPS at the bottom: tap it to see your past trips, newest first, each still opening its timeline.", "Every trip has Lists: To buy, To pack and Before we leave. Type \"buy sun cream\" or \"pack 2 chargers\" and it goes on the right list, in its group (Pharmacy, Documents, Tech…), with \"× 2\"; anything else goes on the list you have open.", "On To pack, \"for the kids\" or \"my …\" says whose it is, and Everyone · Me · Kids shows just theirs. A tick shows at once on the Fold and the Mac and sinks to the bottom; Bought and Packed count how far you are. Press and hold an item (right-click on the Mac) to remove it, with Undo.", "Anything on a trip's To buy is on your shopping list too, marked \"For Barcelona trip\". Tick it in either place (in the shop, or on the trip) and both are ticked, on the Fold and the Mac; if it was already on your shopping list, the trip shares it rather than adding it twice.", "On Before we leave, a time at the end of a job sets a reminder: \"put the bins out at 9pm\" reminds you the night before at 21:00, \"check in online at 06:30\" on the day (\"the night before\" or \"on the day\" choose the day yourself).", "A job's row then says \"Remind Tue 21:00\" and a heads-up comes at that time until you tick it. It moves with the trip's dates, and comes along when you start from a last trip or a template.", "Tap a trip's name on its Lists to say who's going (you, your partner, the kids, named from About you) and when you leave home (\"06:30\"); the dates then say \"4 people\" and the countdown \"leave home 06:30 Wednesday\". With the kids not going, To pack drops its Kids filter.", "A new trip with empty lists offers \"Start from\" your last trip: one tap copies its To buy, To pack and Before we leave, all unticked (Undo takes them off again), and the To buy ones go on your shopping list for the new trip.", "At the foot of a trip's Lists, \"Save as a template for next time\" keeps them (never the ticks) under the trip's name. A new trip's empty lists then offer \"Start from your Lisbon template\" first; press and hold it (right-click on the Mac) to forget it. Saving the same trip again updates its template.", "Ask or Talk to Obi: \"add sun cream to my trip list\", \"pack the passports for Lisbon\" or \"what's left to pack?\". He shows a card with what goes on which list; tap Add (or say yes) and it is added, Undo takes it off again.", "Each list has Obi's suggestions above the add field: what you might have forgotten, from the trip's length, who's going, where it is (passports, GHIC cards and plug adapters abroad), a flight (boarding passes, check in online the night before) and the forecast there once it's known (sun cream, swimwear, coats, an umbrella). Tap one to add it, or Add all; nothing is added until you tap.", "\"Not now\" puts that card's suggestions away for this trip on the Fold and the Mac. Anything already on the lists, ticked or not, is never suggested, and once a trip has lists a few things from your last trip are offered too.", "The groups on a trip's lists are yours. Tap ⋯ on a thing (or press and hold it) to change its name, how many, whose it is, or its group (New group… makes one); right-click it on the Mac for Change… and Move to.", "Tap ⋯ on a group's heading (right-click on the Mac) to rename it, move it up or down, or delete it; its things go to Other, with Undo. \"+ Group\" at the foot adds a group. A template saved from the trip keeps your groups.", "A thing goes into one of your own groups when its words match (a \"Kitchen\" group catches a blender). When nothing matches, \"Put it in:\" offers your groups under the field for a few seconds.", "Press and hold a thing on a trip's list and drag it onto another group: that group's heading lights up and the thing moves there when you let go. Press and hold a group's heading and drag it to put your groups in the order you pack. On the Mac, drag a thing onto a heading, or a heading onto another."),
            fold = HelpPlace.TRIPS,
            foldWhere = "Ask → Life → Trips",
            mac = HelpPlace.TRIPS,
            macWhere = "Ask → Life → Trips",
            macHow = null,
            data = true,
        ),
